# Harsh Mentor: "Whenever an opponent activates an ability of an artifact, creature, or land on the battlefield, if it isn't a
# mana ability, this creature deals 2 damage to that player." Bot2 taps Moxen, Mind Stone and Llanowar Elves for mana (nothing:
# mana abilities are excluded by the card, CR 605.1a: their activation is an event too (CR 605.3), and the trigger refuses it),
# activates Ajani Resolute's 0 (a planeswalker's ability, not an artifact's, creature's or land's:
# nothing, so Bot2 is at 21), forestcycles Generous Ent (a creature card's ability, but from a hand, not on the battlefield - the
# ruling: nothing) and then activates Mind Stone's "{1}, {T}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card". Mind Stone is in the graveyard
# once the cost is paid, and it was an artifact on the battlefield as it last was (CR 113.7a): Mentor's trigger goes on the stack
# above the draw (CR 603.3) and resolves first (Bot2 at 19 with the draw still on the stack). Bot1's own Figure of Destiny
# activation on turn 3 is no opponent's: Bot1 stays at 20.

